## E2E Testing (Playwright)

**Setup**:
```bash
pnpm add -D @playwright/test
```

**E2E Test Example**:
```typescript
import { test, expect } from '@playwright/test';

test.describe('Authentication Flow', () => {
  test('user can sign in with wallet', async ({ page }) => {
    // Navigate to app
    await page.goto('http://localhost:3000');

    // Click connect wallet
    await page.click('text=Connect Wallet');

    // Select MetaMask
    await page.click('text=MetaMask');

    // Wait for wallet connection
    await page.waitForSelector('text=0x', { timeout: 10000 });

    // Verify connected
    expect(await page.textContent('button')).toContain('0x');
  });

  test('displays error on failed authentication', async ({ page }) => {
    await page.goto('http://localhost:3000/signin');

    // Trigger auth without connecting wallet
    await page.click('text=Sign In');

    // Verify error message
    await expect(page.locator('text=Please connect your wallet')).toBeVisible();
  });
});
```

## Best Practices

### ✅ DO (Backend):
- Write table-driven tests for multiple scenarios
- Use testify/assert for cleaner assertions
- Mock external dependencies (database, APIs)
- Test error cases, not just happy paths
- Use testcontainers for integration tests
- Run tests with race detector
- Aim for >80% code coverage
- Test edge cases and boundary conditions

### ✅ DO (Frontend):
- Test user interactions, not implementation
- Use React Testing Library queries (getByRole, getByText)
- Mock API calls with MSW
- Test accessibility (screen readers)
- Test loading and error states
- Use Playwright for critical user flows
- Test with different viewport sizes
- Verify i18n translations

### ❌ DON'T:
- Test implementation details
- Skip error case tests
- Write flaky tests
- Use sleep/timeouts instead of waitFor
- Test third-party libraries
- Skip cleanup in tests
- Ignore warnings in test output
- Write tests that depend on execution order
- Use snapshot testing for everything

## Test Coverage Goals

- **Backend**: Minimum 80% coverage
- **Frontend**: Minimum 70% coverage
- **Critical paths**: 100% coverage (auth, payments)
- **Utilities**: 90%+ coverage

## CI/CD Integration

**GitHub Actions**:
```yaml
name: Tests

on: [push, pull_request]

jobs:
  backend-tests:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v3
      - uses: actions/setup-go@v4
        with:
          go-version: '1.21'
      - name: Run tests
        run: |
          cd apps/backend
          go test -race -coverprofile=coverage.out ./...
      - name: Upload coverage
        uses: codecov/codecov-action@v3

  frontend-tests:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v3
      - uses: pnpm/action-setup@v2
      - uses: actions/setup-node@v3
      - name: Install dependencies
        run: pnpm install
      - name: Run tests
        run: pnpm test:coverage
      - name: Upload coverage
        uses: codecov/codecov-action@v3
```

